# Live UI Required — Scripting & Healing

## Rule

Agents that **generate**, **update**, or **heal** Playwright automation **must** discover and validate locators against the **live application under test** via Playwright MCP (`generator_setup_page` / `planner_setup_page` / `test_debug` + `browser_*`).

Figma HTML, FSD, Excel, heal shells, and fixtures are **supporting references only**. They must not replace live DOM discovery when the app is reachable.

## Must do

1. Call setup once (`generator_setup_page` or `planner_setup_page` / `test_debug` for heal) with the project seed.
2. Derive and navigate to the case’s **real module URL** (path under `BASE_URL`), not only the host root and never a route copied from another module.
3. Use `browser_snapshot` / `browser_evaluate` / `browser_generate_locator` before writing or changing selectors.
4. Exercise critical flows live before finalizing POM methods (open create, library, enable/disable, etc. as required by the task).
5. Record evidence (snapshot paths, control labels, aria names) in the change summary.
6. Update `objectrepositories/` and POM from **live** labels; keep heal-shell fallbacks secondary and aligned to live when possible.
7. **Single MCP owner:** only one agent session may drive Playwright MCP for a given generation/healing run. Parent must not keep calling `browser_*` while a background child also generates/heals on MCP. QA pipeline Generate defaults to in-parent ownership (see `qa-automation-pipeline` Single MCP owner rules).

## 100% invocation coverage

- **Generator:** every eligible UI case assigned to the invocation must have live route, control/action, expected-result-target, and locator evidence. `liveUiValidatedCaseIds` must equal `eligibleUiCaseIds`; `liveUiCoveragePercent=100`.
- **Strict gate fields (mandatory per batch 1–6):** each `liveUiEvidenceByCase` entry must include `moduleUrl`, on-disk `evidenceReferences[]` (≤3 cases per ref), and `controlsOrActionsValidated[]`. Run `npm run qa:audit-live-ui-evidence` after each batch Generate; legacy-only `snapshotPaths`/`controlsVerified` without strict fields fail audit.
- **Healer:** every case whose code is changed must have pre-fix and post-fix evidence on its correct live module route. `liveUiValidatedHealedCaseIds` must equal changed case IDs; `liveUiHealingCoveragePercent=100`.
- Opening the live app once, checking a representative subset, or reusing evidence from an unrelated/stale browser page is not 100% coverage.
- Do **not** attach the same snapshot/evidence reference to many cases with rewritten control text. The completion gate fails `noBulkLiveUiEvidence` when any reference is reused above the limit (default 3) or claims conflicting `moduleUrl`s.
- Do **not** shrink `eligibleUiCaseIds` to force 100% coverage. Exclude only via `blockedUiCaseIds` + `blockedUiReasons` (`honestUiEligibility`).
- Any missing per-case evidence makes the invocation **Incomplete/Blocked**, never Done.

## Host root vs SPA routes

This AML host may return a generic Apache/`It works!` page at **`BASE_URL/`** while the real Clari5 SPA loads on **module paths**.  

- **Do not** mark live UI Blocked solely because the root path shows Apache.
- **Do** open the module route(s) for the Excel/FSD under test and confirm the Clari5/AML UI (title, sidebar, or module content).
- Block only if the **module URL** fails or still shows a non-app page after navigation.

## Must not do

- Skip live exploration because Figma/Excel “already define” labels.
- Rely only on heal/mock injected UI when the live app responds.
- Mark generation or healing **complete** if live UI was not opened and inspected (unless blocked — see below).
- Invent locators from memory or docs without a live snapshot for that screen.
- Treat `BASE_URL` root Apache alone as proof the AML app is down.

## When live UI is blocked

If the app is down or MCP browser fails:

1. Status = **Blocked** (not Done).
2. State the exact blocker (URL tried, error, missing env).
3. Do **not** silently substitute Figma-only / heal-only locator updates as final.
4. Optionally draft offline notes, but do not claim scripts are live-validated.

**Note:** While login is bypassed, missing `EMAIL`/`PASSWORD` is **not** a live-UI blocker — navigate with `BASE_URL` only.

## Applies to

- `playwright-test-generator` / `.cursor/agents/test-generator.agent.md`
- `playwright-test-healer` / `.cursor/agents/test-healer.agent.md`
- `qa-automation-pipeline` six-batch Generate stage (cumulative 100% of eligible
  UI cases) and its one permitted healer cycle per batch
- Any ad-hoc agent asked to update specs, POM, or locators

For `qa-automation-pipeline`, `liveUiValidatedCaseIds` must cover every eligible UI case and `liveUiCoveragePercent` must equal **100**. These agents also enforce complete Excel/plan case coverage and forbid Figma/mock-only Final generation.
